---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About VibePrompt"
  description="VibePrompt is a curated, copy-ready prompt library for AI coding tools — Claude Code, Cursor, Lovable and Jev. Built by developers, for developers who ship."
>
  <nav class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4"><a href="/" class="hover:text-foreground">Home</a> / About</nav>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-5">About VibePrompt</h1>
  <div class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
    <p>
      VibePrompt is a curated library of copy-ready prompts for AI coding tools. Every prompt on this site follows three rules:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
      <li><strong>Copy-ready</strong> — replace the placeholders and paste it. No multi-step setup articles before you can use it.</li>
      <li><strong>Tested patterns</strong> — each prompt encodes a workflow (debugging contracts, scaffolding sequences, decision rubrics), not a one-liner.</li>
      <li><strong>Honest scope</strong> — we say which tool and which situation a prompt is for, and when not to use it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We cover Claude Code, Cursor, Lovable and Jev, and add new prompts weekly. When a new AI coding tool starts trending, we add a section for it —
      that is the whole point of a prompt library in 2026.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
